"""Additional walkthroughs and controls, checked against the current UI source."""

# (Screenshot, title, explanation, controls, example.) Each entry gets its own page.
ADDITIONS = [
('01-account-menu', 'Your identity travels with the work.',
 'The account menu identifies the acting officer, agency and role. Those details determine which work areas the interface offers and which records the service may return. The screenshot shows the demonstration account picker; an operational deployment uses its configured sign-in service.',
 ['Open the avatar to check the active identity before starting work.', 'The demonstration picker changes the synthetic user so different roles can be explored. It is a demo facility, not the production sign-in flow.', 'Production sign-in uses the configured OIDC provider. Sign out ends that session; the theme control changes the workspace appearance.'],
 'A demonstration can move from the investigating officer to the supervisor to show both sides of an approval.'),
('01-role-refused', 'Access decisions stay visible.',
 'A copied navigation link does not grant permission. When the selected role cannot use a screen, Mosaic explains that refusal and offers a route back to the overview. Record-level requests are also checked by the service.',
 ['Navigation shows the work areas offered to the active role.', 'The refusal screen is different from an empty result: the user is not authorised for this work area.', 'Back to overview returns to the available work queue without changing identity or permissions.'],
 'An oversight officer can inspect access events without receiving the investigator’s personal-record workspace.'),
('03-case-close', 'Close a case with its outcome.',
 'Closing a case records the outcome and moves the case out of active investigation. The close dialog asks what happened, such as a filed charge-sheet or a closure report. Retention is then governed by the case’s configured retention date and any legal hold.',
 ['Enter the outcome in the close-case dialog, then confirm or cancel.', 'Legal hold and Lift legal hold are separate case actions. Each asks for a recorded reason.', 'Oversight shows scheduled, due and held cases. An authorised retention action removes eligible case-bound data and records a purge manifest.'],
 'A supervisor records the closure outcome while retaining the case under a reasoned hold when further proceedings require it.'),
('03-case-evidence', 'An exhibit keeps its history.',
 'The evidence locker lists sealed files with their descriptions, source details and fingerprints. The file and its custody history are connected, allowing a reviewer to check what was received and the actions recorded against it.',
 ['Select an exhibit to inspect its custody chain, then close the chain panel to return to the locker.', 'Download retrieves the exhibit through the case workflow and records the access.', 'Verify checks the stored bytes against the recorded fingerprint. A matching hash supports an integrity check; it does not establish that the original content was truthful.'],
 'Before preparing a release, an officer checks the uploaded bank statement’s fingerprint and reviews its custody events.'),
('03-report-editor-2', 'Choose what each report item prints.',
 'A report is assembled from structured blocks. A record block can include particulars, phones and accounts, addresses and criminal history. Its officer’s note adds interpretation beneath the sourced material, keeping the narrative beside the facts it discusses.',
 ['Use the per-item checkboxes under What to print to include the relevant record sections.', 'Insert a heading, free text, a record, an exhibit, a pattern lead, an area search or links between records.', 'Move blocks up or down, or remove them from this draft. Removing a report block does not delete its source record.'],
 'An intelligence summary can show the relevant accounts and a short officer’s note without printing every available field.'),
('03-report-editor-3', 'Keep the draft under control.',
 'The report title, text and block order are editable. Unsaved changes are shown explicitly. Saving preserves the draft; exporting produces a fixed copy for a named reader. If a competing update is detected, the editor presents a reload action.',
 ['Save stores the edited draft. Returning to All reports or opening Export PDF first saves pending edits through the editor flow.', 'Already inserted records are disabled in the insertion list to avoid accidental duplicate blocks.', 'The draft’s creator can discard it. Reload refreshes a conflicting draft so the officer can review the current version before continuing.'],
 'The officer arranges the account evidence before the narrative conclusion, saves the draft and exports the reviewed copy.'),
('06-watchlist-search', 'A useful search keeps working.',
 'A saved search retains a query for the active case. When it is evaluated again as the work queue loads, newly visible matching records can reach the queue and this saved-search view. It uses the records available to the case, not an unrestricted external search.',
 ['Select a saved search to read its name, reason and visible results.', 'Mark the results reviewed so the case team can distinguish new material from material already read.', 'Stop searching ends the saved search with a recorded reason. Start a new saved search from Explorer.'],
 'A saved family-name search can bring a newly ingested matching record to the team’s attention on its next evaluation.'),
('07-network-list', 'Find a record without searching the canvas.',
 'The record list provides a searchable alternative to locating a small node in a dense graph. Selecting a row focuses that record and its available relationships. It also provides a usable selection route when a graphical view is difficult to navigate.',
 ['Toggle Record list and search, then type a name or reference.', 'Click a record to select it; multiple selection allows actions on more than one loaded record.', 'Fit to view, zoom, labels, spacing and rearrange change the presentation. Remove from this view only hides a node from the current canvas.'],
 'In a network with many accounts, an analyst searches the last digits of an account reference and opens its inspector.'),
('07-network-types', 'Arrange the network around the question.',
 'Layouts organise the same available records in different ways. By record type places similar objects together; money flow follows transfers; neighbourhood focuses on the selected record. Presentation controls help the officer read the network without changing the underlying facts.',
 ['Choose Structure, Money flow, By record type, By community, Neighbourhood or Force-directed.', 'Filter relationship layers and record families to concentrate on money, communications or assets.', 'Neighbourhood depth and path methods work within loaded records. They do not enlarge the case’s access rights.'],
 'The analyst groups accounts and companies by type to see which people control several organisations.'),
('07-network-community', 'Read the structure, then inspect the evidence.',
 'Network structure analysis works over all loaded records, including those currently hidden on the canvas. Its groups, routes and weak connections describe the available graph. They help an officer choose what to inspect next.',
 ['Groups identifies communities. Go-betweens lists records on routes between other records.', 'Records holding it together, Only links between parts and Separate parts identify articulation points, bridges and disconnected components.', 'Tightest group and Loops expose a dense core and directed cycles. Mixed-link cycles are not proof of round-tripping; transaction chronology must be checked separately.'],
 'A shared handset may appear as a connection between two groups. The officer opens its source records before interpreting that position.'),
('08-dossier-overview-2', 'Understand the case assessment.',
 'The lower overview explains the subject’s position in this case and shows related alerts. Its facts refer to the case network: account activity, transaction timing and recorded relationships. A position in this network is an investigative pointer, not a general risk score stored on the person.',
 ['Read the evidence behind the case assessment rather than relying on the rank alone.', 'Follow the account or relationship reference to inspect its source-backed details.', 'Use the neighbouring alerts to choose a focused money trail or network question.'],
 'An officer checks the account-level reasons behind a high position before adding a lead to the case board.'),
('08-dossier-network', 'An entity’s relationships, in context.',
 'The Network tab embeds the graph inside the dossier. It lets the investigator move from identity to relationships without starting another search. The familiar layout, filtering and selection controls are available around the entity’s loaded neighbourhood. In this example, selecting Zenova Trading Pvt Ltd exposes its links to directors, its bank account, its registered address and a case record.',
 ['Change relationship layers to compare calls, accounts, companies and other connections.', 'Select a related record for inspection or open its dossier.', 'Use the full Network action when a larger workspace is needed for the same investigation.'],
 'After reading a company’s financials, the officer selects the company in its network and examines its directors and account relationships.'),
('08-dossier-unmask', 'Protected values need an explicit step.',
 'A masked value is shown as protected rather than absent. Where policy permits, the officer can request an unmask action with a written reason. The service still checks the officer, case and field; entering a reason alone does not grant access.',
 ['Choose Unmask on the protected value to open the dialog.', 'State the case-specific reason, then confirm or cancel.', 'The access decision is recorded. An identifier stored only in partial form cannot be reconstructed by unmasking it.'],
 'An investigator records why a protected contact value is needed to follow an authorised line of enquiry.'),
('09-money-in', 'Trace where the money came from.',
 'The incoming direction reverses the question: which accounts or parties supplied funds to the starting record? The diagram groups the traced transfers by hop, while the side panel ranks originators by traced value.',
 ['Switch from Where it went to Where it came from.', 'Adjust hop count and the minimum-transfer amount to choose the extent of the trace.', 'Open an originator’s dossier to inspect the underlying person or company, then compare its other links.'],
 'Starting with a recipient account, an analyst follows incoming transfers to identify the records feeding it.'),
('09-money-accounts', 'Keep separate accounts visible.',
 'By account preserves each account as a separate bar. By party combines accounts associated with the same person or company. Comparing the two views distinguishes an overall recipient from the individual accounts through which transfers moved.',
 ['Use By account when the exact account route matters; use By party to compare account holders.', 'Hover a bar to isolate its flows. Select a linked holder or recipient to open the dossier.', 'Read the flagged accounts and end points beside the diagram. Hop and threshold limits can stop a trace before its ultimate destination.'],
 'Several accounts belonging to one holder may appear as one party but remain distinct in the account view.'),
('10-connect-start', 'Start with one subject, then choose the second.',
 'Connections can begin with one record. The screen shows available associations, conduct flags and supporting relationship evidence. Selecting a second record asks for the chain joining them within the case’s permitted reach.',
 ['Search the From field for a person, account, phone or company.', 'Choose a second result, an associate or a record in the connection network.', 'Clear the second record to return to the first subject’s associations. Open either dossier to review its underlying facts.'],
 'An officer starts from an account holder, selects an associated company and inspects the records that connect them.'),
('11-globe-zoom', 'Move from the country to the street.',
 'The map presents both broad flows and local relationships. Clusters keep nearby records readable at a wide scale. Selecting a cluster or zooming in reveals the records and links that share that location.',
 ['Switch map mode and use the rotation control when exploring the globe.', 'Toggle layers, zoom and select a record to bring its relationships forward.', 'Use the selection panel to open a dossier, money trail or network. A mapped registered address is not proof of presence at a particular time.'],
 'A cross-border transfer can be followed from the national view into the city where its linked company is registered.'),
('11-area-panel', 'Set the place, window and reason.',
 'An area search asks which visible records place vehicles, phones or travellers inside a circle during a stated period. The officer chooses a centre, radius, start and end time, and the reason for searching.',
 ['Search for a recorded toll plaza, camera or tower, or use Pick on map.', 'Set the radius in kilometres and the time window. The reason is retained with the search.', 'If there is no recorded sensor in the circle, the screen explains why it cannot place anyone there. Adjust the circle when appropriate.'],
 'To examine an incident near a toll plaza, the officer narrows the time window to the relevant evening before running the search.'),
('11-area-results-2', 'Read sightings alongside their limits.',
 'Area results separate vehicles, phones and travellers, with the recorded locations and time range behind each result. Registered residents are presented separately: an address is different evidence from a toll read or a tower-associated call.',
 ['Select a result to inspect the reads or bookings that placed it in the area.', 'Open the record’s dossier or its owner’s network when that identity is visible to the case.', 'Watch this area retains the circle for new activity. A report can include the saved area-search result.'],
 'A vehicle read can support a question about its movement; a person’s registered address alone cannot establish that they were there.'),
('12-explore', 'Browse records and aggregate incidents.',
 'Explorer combines text search, object-type selection and record inspection. Police roles can also explore aggregate incident figures by month, district, section of law and kind. Selecting a chart category narrows the incident view.',
 ['Search by name, phone, vehicle or case reference and optionally choose an object type.', 'Open a result to read its properties, sources, marking and links. Add to case and unmask actions require the applicable permission and a reason.', 'Save search asks for a name and a reason so that later matching records can appear in the work queue.'],
 'A police analyst starts with incidents in one district, narrows by month and opens the relevant records for the active case.'),
('13-studio-changes', 'See exactly what publication would change.',
 'The Changes view separates new records, gaps filled, corroborated values, conflicts and learned name spellings. These are proposed operations, allowing the reviewer to understand the effect before publication.',
 ['Compare the incoming value with the value already on record.', 'Read conflicts as items for review rather than permission to overwrite the existing value.', 'Check the legal order and proposer’s note alongside the proposed operations before submitting.'],
 'A bank extract may confirm an existing PAN while adding an address and flagging a conflicting date for review.'),
('13-studio-diary', 'Turn a document into traceable tags.',
 'The studio can prepare narrative material as well as structured extracts. The original text remains visible while tagged identifiers, amounts, dates and places identify the parts that can be compared with existing records.',
 ['Read the text and the highlighted spans together; the tags point back to their location in the document.', 'Select a linked identifier to inspect the matching record when authorised.', 'A written name is linked only when supporting identifiers on the same page agree with the recorded person.'],
 'An officer reviewing a seized diary checks the account number beside a written name before accepting the suggested link.'),
('13-studio-proposed', 'Freeze the proposal for another officer.',
 'Submitting an intake records its proposed changes, legal order and explanatory note for review. The proposal list makes its state visible to the case team while keeping publication separate from preparation.',
 ['Review the proposed row counts and operations before submitting.', 'Use Proposals in my cases to open the submitted proposal and inspect its state.', 'The proposer cannot approve their own intake, including when the proposer is also a supervisor.'],
 'The preparing officer submits the cleaned bank extract; the case supervisor reviews the same frozen proposal.'),
('13-studio-review', 'Approve, reject or revert with a reason.',
 'A different supervisor in the case reviews the proposed operations and legal order. Approval publishes the recorded changes. Rejection keeps the proposal from publication; a later revert undoes the published operations through the recorded workflow.',
 ['Enter the decision reason before Approve and publish or Reject.', 'After publication, Revert this publish also requires a reason.', 'Case on map opens the geographic context. Re-run patterns asks the detector workflow to consider the newly available records.'],
 'A supervisor rejects an intake whose order does not support the proposed material and records the reason for the preparing officer.'),
('14-review-pair', 'Compare the source records before deciding.',
 'A proposed match presents two records side by side and explains their agreement and disagreement. Common names carry less distinguishing value than rare names. Matching identifiers and source context help the reviewer reach a considered decision.',
 ['Choose a waiting pair and compare the original names, family details, birth information, district and available identifiers.', 'Read Why they were paired and the field-level evidence.', 'Record a reason and choose Same person or Different people. A decision is an explicit review action, not a consequence of opening the pair.'],
 'Two similar names can describe different people when their birth details and phone records disagree.'),
('15-faces-empty', 'Begin with a still held by the case.',
 'Face search begins with the image and the order or seizure memo under which it was obtained. The preview distinguishes a selected file from an image already added as case evidence.',
 ['Choose the probe image and inspect the preview before sending it.', 'Enter the legal order or seizure memo.', 'Add as evidence and find faces seals the still through the evidence workflow before detecting faces. If none is found, the screen asks for a clearer or closer image.'],
 'An officer selects a synthetic CCTV still for the demonstration and checks that the intended frame is shown.'),
('15-faces-found', 'Choose one face from the still.',
 'A still may contain more than one face. Detection marks the available faces, allowing the officer to select the intended subject rather than treating the whole image as one query.',
 ['Inspect the detected faces on the original still.', 'Choose one face and enter the reason for searching it.', 'Search the chosen face compares that selection against photographs the active case may access.'],
 'When a still contains two people, the officer selects the relevant face and records why it is being compared.'),
('15-faces-confirm', 'A second officer records the decision.',
 'Candidate results remain proposals. The pending list lets another officer of the same case review a proposed match and record a confirmation or rejection with a reason. The searching officer cannot confirm their own search.',
 ['Inspect the candidate photograph, similarity, source and visible dossier information.', 'Enter the reason for the decision before choosing Confirm or Reject.', 'Confirmed matches retain the human decision; rejected candidates are not promoted into an identification.'],
 'The second officer checks the candidate against the evidence and rejects an apparent resemblance that is not adequately supported.'),
('16-cop-dispatch', 'Record the response against the alert.',
 'The dispatch form records a resource, quantity and destination district against the selected disaster context. The dispatch log makes recorded allocations visible in the control-room workflow.',
 ['Read the alert’s timing, severity, mapping basis and affected districts.', 'Choose the resource, enter its quantity and select the destination district.', 'Dispatch adds the entry to the log. It records the allocation in Mosaic; it is not evidence that a physical delivery has occurred.'],
 'A control-room operator records relief kits allocated to a flood-affected district and reviews the resulting log entry.'),
('17-oversight-filtered', 'Answer who accessed a particular record.',
 'Audit filters narrow the trail by user or record identifier. Each returned event carries its time, actor, action, case and purpose, number of records, outcome and details. Refused actions remain relevant to the review.',
 ['Enter a user ID, a record ID or both, then Apply filters.', 'Compare the recorded purpose with the action and its outcome.', 'Check the chain state and seal the daily root when required. Publishing that root outside the system is a separate operational step.'],
 'An auditor examines access to one record and distinguishes allowed look-ups from refused requests.'),
('18-admin-quality', 'Return source problems to their owner.',
 'Source data quality lists issues discovered while loading records. Each entry connects an issue with the affected record and its source, helping the data steward route corrections to the organisation responsible for the original material.',
 ['Read the record identifier, issue description and source together.', 'Use these references to investigate the original extract and coordinate a correction.', 'The register reports issues; it is not a bulk editing interface for silently changing the source records.'],
 'A district-name mapping problem can be reported to the source owner with the exact record reference.'),
]

EXTRAS = {
 '02-overview-crime': ['Refresh reloads the work queue. Category filters and Find in queue narrow it to approvals, requests, watches, saved searches or refusals.', 'Recent decisions records the response to earlier requests. Work-queue times use IST; audit timestamps identify UTC explicitly.'],
 '01-search': ['Use Ctrl+K to focus search, arrow keys to select a result, Enter to open it and Escape to close the results. Search suggestions follow the active identity and case.'],
 '02-overview-supervisor': ['A request card carries the decision action and recorded reason. Approval is available only where the acting supervisor satisfies the relevant role, agency, membership and two-person checks.'],
 '03-case-board': ['Shared with other cases links to the cases the officer may access. The network counts describe the loaded case network rather than a count of convictions or established findings.'],
 '03-case-evidence-exports': ['Choose Case report (PDF), Report (HTML) or the court evidence pack ZIP. Specify the recipient and release clearance. The pack includes exhibits, custody records, the draft certificate and a hash manifest.'],
 '05-alerts': ['Filter by typology and severity. Select one alert to read the detailed finding, then use Open dossier, Trace funds or Network. Alert priority helps order review; it is not a finding about a person.'],
 '07-network-inspector': ['Path choices include shortest connection in either direction, three alternative routes, shortest directed path, money-only path and maximum flow. A capacity calculation is not proof that a particular amount actually travelled along that route.'],
 '08-dossier-overview': ['Where multiple photographs exist, Previous photograph and Next photograph show each image with its source. Copy reference copies the record identifier for use in a case note.'],
 '08-dossier-financials': ['Filter to one account and set Min ₹ to hide smaller transactions. The table preserves date, direction, amount, payment channel, narration, counterparty and reference.'],
 '08-dossier-timeline': ['Use Newer and the available paging controls to move through dated events. Open an entry to inspect the record rather than treating the timeline caption as the whole evidence.'],
 '13-studio-cleanup': ['Suggested steps resets the clean-up recipe. Apply clean-up previews the configured steps. Cells changed, Quarantined and Duplicates expose separate consequences of the recipe.'],
 '13-studio-fields': ['Default mapping restores the suggested mapping; Apply mapping previews the edited one. Unmapped fields and policy-blocked record classes are explicit.'],
 '13-studio-matching': ['Filter All, On record, Probable or New. A lens can narrow the rows from a check; clear the lens to restore the full list.'],
 '13-studio-checks': ['Show rows opens the records behind a check. Checked and Dismiss record the reviewer’s disposition of an individual pattern. Links and place views use the same proposed extract.'],
 '18-admin-library': ['Expand a detector card to read the tactics addressed, innocent look-alikes, blind spots and references. Version, scope and mission tracks identify where the detector belongs.', 'The Pattern tests and Record matching tabs provide diagnostic review tools for maintainers. This book describes their role without reproducing benchmark tables or test results.'],
}

EXAMPLES = {
 '01': 'The officer checks the active case, then opens the relevant item from the work queue or searches for a known reference.',
 '02': 'An investigating officer and supervisor use the same case context while seeing the actions available to their respective roles.',
 '03': 'The team follows a line of enquiry from its case records into evidence and a reviewed, recipient-specific report.',
 '19': 'The officer reviews the generated document and completes the required human checks before using it outside the workspace.',
 '04': 'An officer checks the lead’s evidence and alternative explanations before requesting a case or dismissing it with a reason.',
 '05': 'An analyst opens the flagged account, inspects its transactions and traces the relevant transfers.',
 '06': 'The case team reviews newly visible activity, records that it has been read and stops a watch when its reason no longer applies.',
 '07': 'The investigator selects a relationship in the network and opens the records that support it before interpreting the connection.',
 '08': 'The officer moves from the subject’s summary into the relevant tab, then checks the source behind the fact being used.',
 '09': 'The analyst compares the direction and extent of the trace with the original transactions before describing the money route.',
 '10': 'Two subjects are selected and the connecting records are reviewed one step at a time.',
 '11': 'The officer compares the mapped record with its time and source before using it to support a location-based enquiry.',
 '12': 'A useful case-scoped query is saved so the next evaluation can surface newly available matching records.',
 '13': 'An extract is prepared and inspected before a separate supervisor decides whether the proposed changes should be published.',
 '14': 'A reviewer compares the two original records and records a reason for treating them as the same person or different people.',
 '15': 'A still becomes evidence, one face is searched with a reason and a different officer reviews the candidate decision.',
 '16': 'The operator checks an ingested alert, its affected area and nearby resources before recording a response.',
 '17': 'The auditor follows an access event back to its user, case, stated purpose and recorded outcome.',
 '18': 'The data steward reads the documented behaviour of a detector or routes a source issue to the owner of the affected records.',
}
